# The three loops over the index space compute from the index (and an
# offset) alone, so their bodies only compute and they are structured;
# after the vectorization they run on the target's lanes, and after
# idr-narrow-lanes each loop that computes 64-bit lanes is the 64-bit
# version beside one computing them in 32 bits, under a bound on n and the
# offset that this fixture's input is below (linarray-lanes-narrow) or
# above (linarray-lanes-wide), a negative offset above it either way: both
# versions must give the numbers of 64-bit lanes. The structuring and the
# vectorization group, idr-narrow-lanes among it, each run over the
# functions in a group, which dumps no module: each property is read at
# the first step after its group.
eliminate-empty-tensors: structured-loops
idr-returned-arguments: vectorized narrowed-lanes
